{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB Annual General Adjustment cap","requirement":"The Rent Board may not approve an Annual General Adjustment above 5%; if the Consumer Price Index formula yields a higher figure, the annual rent increase for fully covered units is capped at 5%.","key_value":"5% maximum annual AGA","coverage_conditions":"Fully covered rental units under Berkeley's Rent Ordinance; the Rent Board sets the AGA each year by a Consumer Price Index formula.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"fully covered units"},"exemptions":"Landlords with banked (unused) AGAs may still raise rent above 5% to reach the rent ceiling.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The maximum AGA is 5%. This means that, if the formula in the Rent Ordinance results in an AGA that is greater than 5%, the AGA approved by the Board for that year can be no more than 5%.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB coverage of government-owned or -subsidized units","requirement":"Landlords of government-owned or -subsidized rental units must register them with the Rent Board as fully or partially covered and pay an annual registration fee; fully covered units have a rent ceiling.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Government-owned or -subsidized units, including Section 8, Shelter Plus Care, VASH, LIHTC, HOME and others; full or partial coverage depends on unit type and whether federal or state law exempts the unit from rent control.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"government-owned or -subsidized rental units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Government-owned or -subsidized rental units become either fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB shared kitchen or bath exemption","requirement":"A unit where the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord is exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental units in which the tenant shares kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord; the exemption turns on the landlord residing on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"landlord resides on the same property"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Where the tenant shares a kitchen or bath facilities with the landlord, the unit will be exempt from the Rent Ordinance only if the landlord lived in a unit on the same property at the start of the tenancy.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB limits capital improvement rent petitions to completed work","requirement":"A landlord may petition for a rent increase only for capital improvements that are already completed; petitions to have rent increases preliminarily authorized for planned capital improvements are no longer allowed.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Fully and partially covered rental units under the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"covered units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"Landlords can only file a petition for rent increases for completed capital improvements (they can no longer petition to have rent increases preliminarily authorized for planned capital improvements).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB nonpayment eviction threshold","requirement":"A landlord may evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent only if the tenant owes at least one month's Fair Market Rent for an equivalent-size unit in the Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD metro area for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","key_value":"1 month FMR (Oakland-Fremont HUD metro)","coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance who face eviction for nonpayment of rent.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"fully or partially covered units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"For a landlord to evict a tenant for nonpayment of rent, the tenant must owe an amount of rental debt equal to or greater than one month of the Fair Market Rent (FMR) value for a unit of equivalent size in the metro area Oakland-Fremont, CA HUD Metro FMR as determined by the US Department of Housing and Urban Development for the fiscal year in which the rent is demanded.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB bars eviction for refusing a substantially similar lease","requirement":"A landlord may not evict a tenant for failing to sign a substantially similar lease when a fixed-term lease expires.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"fully or partially covered units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot evict a tenant for failing to sign a substantially similar lease upon expiration of a fixed-term lease.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB requirements for lease-breach evictions","requirement":"To evict for breach of a material lease term, the term must be mutually agreed, the breach must cause substantial actual damage, the tenant's conduct must be unreasonable, and the pre-eviction notice must describe the term, violation and harm in detail.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance whose landlord alleges a lease violation.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"fully or partially covered units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The landlord’s notice to the tenant to stop the violation (which is required before the landlord can serve an eviction notice) must specify the lease term, and describe the violation and resulting harm in enough detail for a reasonable person to understand.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB eviction notice content and Rent Board filing deadline","requirement":"A termination notice must state that Rent Board advice is available and give its counseling phone number and website; the landlord must file copies of the notice, notice to quit, and summons and complaint with the Rent Board within three business days of service.","key_value":"3 business days","coverage_conditions":"Termination notices and eviction lawsuits for units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"fully or partially covered units"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The landlord must file with the Rent Board a copy of any notice to terminate a tenancy, notice to quit, and summons and complaint no later than three business days after the tenant was served with the document.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D006-01","doc_id":"D006","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Measure BB annual adjustment of owner move-in relocation assistance","requirement":"The Rent Board must make inflationary adjustments each year to the relocation assistance amounts paid for owner move-in evictions.","key_value":"annual inflationary adjustment","coverage_conditions":"Owner move-in eviction relocation assistance payments under the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"owner move-in evictions"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Measure BB (Berkeley Rent Ordinance)","quoted_span":"The Rent Board must make inflationary adjustments to owner move-in eviction relocation assistance amounts each year.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
